  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In a poetic language the author contemplates the world around her. Images and words become parallel languages, where the distinction between ground and sky, past and present collapses. One conceit after another feels its way over the tiny words before sinking deep into the dark of the etching ink to linger, trembling."--Women's Studio Workshop website, http://www.wsworkshop.org/php/details.php?ID=3136 viewed July 31, 2009.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text in this book was written by Abigail Uhteg and was letterpress printed in 8- and 10- point Spectrum types on a Vandercook No. 3. The images are rosin aquatints with etching and drypoint printed on Rives BFK. Chris Petrone made the flax and abaca paper for the cover."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in an edition of 35 signed copies. Art Library's copy is no. 18.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="563" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in dark gray flax and abaca paper, with white title label pasted on front cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
